# Planted bugs for the tenant-isolation model. Each one must make the named check miss its expectation.
run fv-alloy tenant-isolation.als
properties NoCrossTenantRead_AllPathsTenantScoped NoCrossTenantRead_NoRule
file tenant-isolation.als

mutation the tenant predicate compares with the wrong operator and selects every other tenant's rows
detects NoCrossTenantRead_AllPathsTenantScoped
- fun visibleRows[p: Principal, q: QueryPath]: set Row {
-   q in TenantScopedPath => { r: Row | r.tenant = p.tenant } else Row
- }
+ fun visibleRows[p: Principal, q: QueryPath]: set Row {
+   q in TenantScopedPath => { r: Row | r.tenant != p.tenant } else Row
+ }

mutation the router drops the principal's own tenant from what it may read
detects NoCrossTenantRead_NoRule
- fun visibleRows[p: Principal, q: QueryPath]: set Row {
-   q in TenantScopedPath => { r: Row | r.tenant = p.tenant } else Row
- }
+ fun visibleRows[p: Principal, q: QueryPath]: set Row {
+   q in TenantScopedPath => { r: Row | r.tenant = p.tenant } else none
+ }

harmless a comment on TenantScopedPath is reworded
- sig TenantScopedPath in QueryPath {}  -- paths whose SQL carries the tenant predicate
+ sig TenantScopedPath in QueryPath {}  -- the paths that filter by tenant_id
